---
name: computer-use
description: Automate authorized browser UI tasks using Playwright where supported, with user confirmation for consequential actions.
Computer Use
Use this skill when the user asks to automate clicks, typing, scrolling, screenshots, or other browser UI steps.
Capability check
Determine the operating system and whether a browser automation tool, Playwright, and a graphical/browser runtime are actually available.
Distinguish a remote Codex sandbox from the user's local Windows desktop. Never claim direct access to the user's mouse, keyboard, or screen unless an authorized local runtime exists.
If Playwright is unavailable, explain the prerequisite and ask permission before installing dependencies or changing the environment.
Browser workflow
Confirm the target site and the user's desired outcome.
Navigate using an authorized browser context.
Prefer stable accessibility locators (role, label, text) over brittle CSS selectors.
Wait for elements and verify page state before and after each meaningful action.
Capture screenshots or logs to diagnose failures, avoiding sensitive content.
Save outputs in the workspace and summarize exactly what completed and what did not.
Require explicit user approval before purchases, submissions, deletions, account changes, or other consequential actions.
Guardrails
Only automate accounts, websites, and data the user is authorized to access.
Respect website terms and rate limits; do not bypass CAPTCHAs, paywalls, or anti-bot controls.
Never expose passwords, cookies, session tokens, or private data in logs.
Browser automation does not imply control of the user's Windows desktop.
If an action fails, report the error rather than claiming success.
